              "type": "pq-policy-question",
              "settings": {
                "question": "When will I receive my refund?",
                "answer": "<p>After an approved returned product has been received and, where applicable, inspected, we will initiate the approved refund to the original payment method within <strong>1–3 business days</strong>.</p><p>Your bank, card issuer, or payment provider may require additional time to post the refund to your account.</p>"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "returns_refunds_10": {
              "type": "pq-policy-question",
              "settings": {
                "question": "Are customs duties and import charges refunded?",
                "answer": "<p>Because [Store Name] bears the applicable tariffs, customs duties, and import charges covered by our shipping policy, those amounts are generally not separately paid by the customer and therefore do not normally constitute a separate refund item.</p><p>If a customer was required to pay an import charge directly with our authorization, the amount will be reviewed based on the specific circumstances and applicable law.</p>"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "returns_refunds_11": {
              "type": "pq-policy-question",
              "settings": {
                "question": "What should I do with a defective product or battery?",
                "answer": "<p>Do <strong>not</strong> destroy, dispose of, dismantle, or return a defective vehicle, component, or battery unless [Store Name] has provided written instructions.</p><p>After reviewing your claim, we may authorize:</p><ul><li>repair;</li><li>replacement parts;</li><li>product return;</li><li>product replacement;</li><li>refund;</li><li>or approved disposal instructions.</li></ul><p>A battery that is damaged, swollen, leaking, overheated, punctured, or otherwise appears unsafe must not be shipped through a normal parcel-return process unless specifically authorized and prepared in accordance with the applicable dangerous-goods requirements.</p>"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
            "returns_refunds_12": {
              "type": "pq-policy-question",
              "settings": {
                "question": "What happens if the product is damaged during return shipping?",
                "answer": "<p>Customers are responsible for packaging authorized returns carefully and following the provided return instructions.</p><p>Original protective packaging should be used whenever available.</p><p>If a non-defective return is materially damaged because it was improperly packaged or returned contrary to our instructions, the refund may be reduced or refused to the extent permitted by applicable law.</p><p>If damage occurs during a seller-arranged return for a confirmed defect, we will investigate the issue with the return carrier.</p>"
              },
              "blocks": {}
            },
